The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in returns 'I cannot' for both reply texts (1) 'I'm sorry, I cannot do that.' and (2) 'I cannot help; I'm sorry.', whereas the documented rule 'The first refusal phrase the text contains, typographic quotes read as straight ones, or None.' would require 'I'm sorry' for reply (1) and 'I cannot' for reply (2), making the two replies indistinguishable to the check.